# Library Directory

This directory is currently unused by the SmartFires firmware.

## When To Put Code Here

Use `lib/` only when a module is truly reusable and should build as an internal PlatformIO library instead of as part of the application source tree.

Good candidates:

- a protocol helper intended to be shared across multiple firmware workspaces
- a hardware abstraction that needs its own `library.json`
- a standalone utility with clear public headers and tests

Keep code in `src/` instead when it is tightly coupled to the current SmartFires base/node firmware flow.

## Current Recommendation

For this project, new code usually belongs in one of these places first:

- `src/app` for base/node orchestration
- `src/radio` for TDMA, join, ACK, or queue behavior
- `src/sensors` for sensor wrappers
- `src/power` for duty-cycle and battery behavior

Promote code into `lib/` only after a clear reuse boundary appears.
